“Great and Mighty” will bring to Moscow: migrants will save money for a language
While the deputies and human rights activists are arguing that will give a law on mandatory language testing, crooks have already appeared in the country who are selling “fake” certificates
Every year 13 million guest workers come to Moscow, St. St. St. Petersburg and other cities of Russia.
For the most part, these are citizens of Central Asia: Uzbekistan, Tajikistan and Turkmenistan.
Their only goal is to earn money to support families left in their homeland.
From December 1, the law came into force, according to which every labor migrant will be obliged to pass an exam for knowledge of the Russian language.
While this rule applies only for those who intend to work in the field of service, housing and communal services, household and retail.
However, over time - they promise in FMS - tests will become mandatory for all visitors.
At the same time, you will have to pass not only the language, but also Russian history and the basis of the legislation.
The knowledge of the language will have to be confirmed for obtaining and for renewing a work permit.
An exception is valid only for citizens of those countries where Russian is the state language.
Do not fall under the scope of the law and people who managed to obtain certificates and diplomas of education before the collapse of the USSR in 1991.
Benefficiencies, Dominance and Protection of Rights
The network of examination points will work under the auspices of the Pushkin Institute of the Russian Language, the University for Friendship of Peoples, MSU, SPbSU and other Russian universities.
Immigrants will be able to take tests in all cubies; more than 160 such centers have already been opened in Russia.
The initiative to introduce testing was supported by the deputies of the state Duma and the FMS.
But human rights activists, before the law came into force, many times managed to ask in the press a question: and what, in fact, does it give?
What will change the purity of knowledge of the language for both the Russians and for the visitors themselves?
First of all - representatives of the migratory service - this will reduce the number of people who are suffering from "dividual slavery".
Very many people are now talking about the protection of the rights of labor migrants, explains the head of the representative office of the FMS of the Russian Federation in Tajikistan Viktor Sebelev.
The protection of their rights must begin before their departure.
Only the system of organized recruitment will 90% solve the problems of foreign workers.
There are problems in migrants without a profession, an education that does not know a language that does not have a medical examination.
Without an inculgnacy of the language," Sebelev said, "the future immigrant is destined to encounter unscrupulous people who, under the guise of help, put a "voice" into a creepy crumbling bark, where he and dozens of his kind languish languish for months without food and documents, working 12-14 hours a day.
We receive a lot of complaints from our migrants.
“In their homeland, they are promised one thing, and upon arrival they are deceiving, passports are taken away, they do not pay the promised salary”, – confirms the head of the Main Directorate of labor migrating of the MC of the Tajik Tolib Sharipov.
Don't be arguing, sanctuary!
Nevertheless, so far, many citizens of the Central Asian republic, who are going to work in Russia, admit that not only they do not not know the language of the country in which they aspire, but they also write on their own with it with difficulty.
Of course, this is not so much their fault, but trouble: few Turkmens, Uzbeks, Tajiks can afford even a sensible primary education.
After all, their families do not even even feed their children, not to mention to decently dress, shoe and equip them to the school.
Growing before adolescence, such children at the first opportunity go to work.
Difficulty, if it is bad with the knowledge of the language - they are recognized.
Feel humiliated and humiliated.
However, in relation to the law on the language, human rights defenders note one important point.
Testing will be carried out only for those migrants who have legal status.
If there is not a status - there will not be an exam or a follow-up official work.
In the meantime, the majority of guest workers continue to live in Russia illegally.
"Welcome, or Outsiders Are Forgiven Entry"
Many of the visitors argue that it is not so easy to obtain an official status in our country.
The reason - in bureaucratic diapers and all the same linguistic difficulties.
In addition, the legalization costs money: from 12 to 16 thousand rubles.
But false registration can be done quickly and for only one and a half thousand.
Employees of the Russian police know that we mainly have false documents, there is no registration, hence the cases of extortion.
“Awaken a Hundundrate a Hundred, for  Cigarette Cabin, Tei, a Tajik citizen Umed Khhushkadam, said.
"Float, don't be abrupt, buy a painting"
On the very first day of the entry into force of the law on the language it turned out that not only immigrant documents on registration are false.
A number of “fake” certificates of passing of language tests have already been withdrawn by FMS employees.
False papers are sealed on an ordinary color printer.
Of course, they went to the new owners it is not for nothing: each of the migrants, who thus hoped to alleviate the task of passing the tests, paid seven thousand rubles for the document.
This is more than twice as expensive than the procedure of official testing: it will cost an employment immigrant in three thousand.
The main task in the near future - to protect the system from corruption, so that "crusts" could not simply be bought, converge both representatives of the authorities and human rights defenders.
In the meanary, the authorities can promise guest workers who have not been able to be successfully tested from the first time, the time to study the basic language course.
In addition, visitors who do not know Russian will be offered work in areas that do not involve active communication with people.
The interior Ministry does not take into circulation the illegal arms market
The share of crimes with the use of legal weapons is extremely small
The Ministry of internal Affairs of Russia proposes to tighten the law in respect of owners of civilian weapons.
This is the reaction of the authorities to the recent incidents: Push shots at weddings, when there were no victims, and the carnage arranged by the Moscow lawyer Dmitry Vinogradov, as a result of which seven people were killed.
The police want to prohibit the wearing of injuries in public places and to raise the age at which you can get a license for a weapon - from the age of 18 to the age of 21.
The idea was supported by the head of the Duma Committee on security and anti-corruption Irina Yarovaya and promised that amendments to the law on weapons will be submitted to the state Duma in the near future.
Not everyone is satisfied that the Russian authorities are trying to deal with the problem by “tightening the nuts”.
In the network there was an open letter, the authors of which - representatives of various public shooting organizations - demand to abandon the "meaningless tightening".
The percentage of hooliganism with a registered weapon is minimal, said the Russian service of the B-bi-Criminist lawyer Vasily Lesnikov.
According to the statistics of the Ministry of internal Affairs, during the six months of 2012, 142 crimes were carried out with the use of firearms registered in the internal affairs bodies, while during the same period 1168 thousand crimes were recorded.
The authors of the open letter are confident that the tightening of legislation in the field of civilian weapons does not place the offender to go to the “black” market.
Now, according to them, you can find any weapons at a low price in Moscow.
In the meantime, the interior Ministry claims that it is in control of the situation with the proliferation of illegal weapons.
Providers: from factories to officers
“The “black” arms market is replenished through several canals.
