Shiemon Ornest: In concerts we want to accumulate a positive energy
What do you think that in less than a month the end of the world should come?
“It’s only one of the many disturbing news that we, the people, come across so easily.
Along with The Tap Tap, we are constantly joking on this topic and say that we are the only group in the world that will be able to rapproducing enough energy to delay or prevent the end of the world.
Moreover, in December you are going to give an absolutely unique three concerts against the end of the world.
Could you tell your readers in more detail about this?
We are talking about a nationwide fundraising event, which we have been planning for two years.
We decided to take advantage of the marketing potential, which is possessed by the Mayan Calendar, the end of which is announced on December 21 at 11:10.
The day before this event, on December 20 at 21:00 will start three concerts in Pragh, Brno and Ostrava.
They will end, roughly speaking, at the moment when on the island of Kiribati in the Quiet Ocean, whose time zone is 12 hours earlier than in us, the May calendar will be completed.
To whom came up with this idea?
Initially, this was my idea, then we all came up together with our artist Gonze Auguloy.
In addition to the fact that we want to accumulate quite positive energy and to prevent the end of the world, we also want, together with the public, to think about the state in which this world we will convey to our children one day.
On the occasion graduation of the May Calendar, we have created a unique collection of shoe, t-shirts, handbags and original keys against the end of the world. These things can be bought at www.e-tap.cz and thus at the same time provide us with support.
The Tap Tap together with other musicians also performed the anthem against the end of the world, which is called "The End of the World Cancelled".
Will the an anthem at these beneficial concerts already loved by the listeners sounded?
Of course, at the very end, if in the end everything will turn out and the end of the world does not come.
It will smite all performers at all the concerts at the same time.
Hymns at the same time will also sound live on Czech television.
The words to this song were written and played the role of Jesus in Tomas Ganak's clip, participates in Xindl X.
How did you start working with them?
We also cooperate with other persons of Czech cultural life, as we hold many philanthropic events and concerts.
We try to actively involve them in these projects.
It turned out that many people like to work with us, they are interested.
What will the return from the concert against the end of the world go?
On the purchase of equipment for a barrier-free educational center STUDEO, already for the sixth year we have been working with a civil association Tap at the Edlechki Institute.
Lecturers regularly visit students of the schools of the Judlichki Institute and hold fun and interesting events with them.
The students themselves do not have the funds to go to the teachers, and we try in this way to give them this opportunity.
As part of an additional project for additional construction of the Yedlichka Institute in the future there will be a separate building to which we will move with this project.
At each concert there will be several musical groups and performers.
What Were the Selection Criteria?
We tried to draw up a program that will interest all generations, including children.
For example, in Praga will perform Chinaski, Support Lesbiens, Illustratosphere with DAN Bart, The Tap Tap, Marian Bango and Irzi Suhi.
You can find out about all the details at www.kpks.cz.
Are you planning any such “gremonious events” in the future?
In May we will perform for the first time at the festival "Prague spring" and here, of course, we will prepare an interesting program with interesting guests.
Next next year we would be happy to hold a performance at the Czech national house in New York, and I personally, if we are in the United States, I would very much like to speak in Washington and Chicago.
About abroad you have serious plans, you have already acted in Madrid, Brussels, London and Moscow.
The Tap Tap group is a group of people with disabilities.
How do you cope with the darling from the point of view of organization and logistics?
This is not as scary as it seems at first glance.
We have five participants on electric wheelchairs, their strollers need to travel in the luggage compartment, plus a large number of loads and boxes with tools.
Nevertheless, so far they coped with this without a problem. ČSA Czech airlines and British Airways British Airlines have always been excellently prepared for us, which surprised me how many times.
Even in Moscow, from where we recently returned, everything went without any problems.
Thanks to going abroad, you can compare different countries in terms of accessibility, public relations with persons with people with disabilities and so on.
What have you encountered by the moment?
After Madrid, Luxembourg, London and other countries where everything functions better than in us, in Russia we have witnessed what is still at a basic level in the east.
Compared to Prago, there are a lot of barriers in Moscow, there is still an independent movement of a person on an electric stroller electric wheelchair in the city center.
Also, there are no such banal things how to concede the road to a disabled person in an elevator.
Luckily, public organizations have already arisen there, who are trying to draw people's attention to the problems of people with disabilities.
And what, on the other hand, do we constantly need to catch up with advanced countries?
There are a lot of things, the level of fulfillment of which is far behind.
But it is important to clarify that the improvement and improvement of the situation always depends on the efforts of those people concerned.
In London and in Madrid it is quite normal that people with a severe form of disability move independently on the streets, they can go to the toilet, to a museum, and anywhere ...
It is not very prevalent that a large number of people with disabilities take an active part in public life, in this we are a little ahead of them with The Tap Tap!
Respect of the public or barrier-free is one thing, but at a time when there will be well-feminine athletes, artists, actors, politicians or lawyers among us, then everything will really begin to change.
While these are isolated cases - people with a strong volitude.
The Tap Tap band is currently very popular, but let's go back two years ago, what caused you to organise it in 1998?
I went to the Jedlichi Institute as a educator, there were a lot of young people around me who wanted to deal with something.
And since I myself am a musician and I am also playing on a saxophone, together with my colleague he organized an interesting musical circle.
Well, over time, as our presenter Ladya Angelovich says, it got a little out of control (laughs).
Popularity came only in recent years, or am I confusing something?
It's true, it's helped us that we began to join the famous singers and actively work to promote the group.
We came to the conclusion that the work that no one can assess, in fact, does not seem to exist.
Thanks to the funds of the European Union, we are able to afford qualified educators, equipment and so on.
Do you have a goal so well to unleash The Tap Tap?
From the very beginning, I felt their potential in the ability to do something extraordinary.
In the show-business is full of things imitating each other.
This is logical, everything new is taken with caution, and it lasts for a long time.
There are very few very rare things, but I will dare to say that Tap Tap is one.
The first impression of a person who sees us, of course, pity, it is naturally ...
But this palom is completely superfluous, because people with disabilities are not some kind of suffering and all abandoned personalities that we should feel sorry for.
They are people who are able to live a full-fledged life and develop, of course, only on the condition that they have the necessary resources.
I’m saying that if people with a person with a disability does something, it is a shift not only for them, but for the whole society.
Has it ensured the success that you are a strict leader, what do many people consider you to be?
If we want to do the work qualitatively, we need to be uncompromising in many things and keep a certain discipline.
But I don't think it's normal.
Some people come to us with a romantic performance and flies in the clobules, and when they learn that twice a week they should go to rehears, attend preparatory courses and spend a lot of time on the road, lose enthusiasm very quickly very quickly.
But this is the case in any group that wants to work and achieve something.
Currently, there's been a member of The Tap Tap by twenty.
How many of them were at the beginning of 1998?
There's only one Lady Angelovich.
We are an open group, people come and go, it is impossible to prevent it.
For those who have desire and willpower, our doors are always open.
It will take place the day before the expected end of the world, on Thursday 20.12.2012 at 21.
The concert will be held in Prague at the Incheba Stadium, Brno - at the Fléda and Ostrava - in the Plynojem center with the participation of 12 bands and other musicians of the Czech Republic.
At the end of the concert, all three circumstances are connected by a teleconference at the time of the performance of The Tap Tap "Enthose of the World Cancelled".
The purpose of this project is to raise funds in the amount of 25 million kroons to purchase multifunctional barrier-free equipment for the STUDEO educational center at the Jellichki Institute in Prague.
The ticket for the concert costs 400 kroons, for children up to the age of 12 admission is free of charge. Tickets can be bought in advance at Bohemiaticket.
Poland and Solo.
Last week at a ministerial meeting of the European Space Agency of Poland was adopted by the Twentieth member of the European Space Agency as the second country in the former Eastern Bloc (after the Czech Republic, which became a full member of EKA on September 12, 2008).
Poland began close-employed cooperation with ECA in 1994 and for subsequent years took an active part in a number of projects of the agency.
But the Path to Cosmocrat Poland began a lot earlier.
Even before the Second world war, Polish enthusiasts were engaged in flights into space, but this did not always meet with an understanding.
Let me remind me, for example, the lecture of A. Sternfeld, who on December 6, 1933 presented in the Warsaw Astronomical observatory ideas from his innovative "Institution to Cosmonautics".
The ideas of the young engineer (1905) left the audience indulgence, after several years Sternfeld remembered that only Dr. Yang Gadomsky was interested in his work.
In 1934 Sternfeld won the Robert Esno-Peltri and André Luis Hirsch Award for Introducing Astromonopience.
Doctor Yang Gadomskie (1899-1966), mentioned above, later became a great propagandist of astronomy and cosmonautics.
He published in Polish journals hundreds of articles and wrote a number of books devoted to these scientific disciplines.
Gadomsky has become a notorious world propagandist of cosmonautics, and his contribution was appreciated, among other things, that one craters on the far side of the moon was named in his honor.
Already in 1925 in Poland was built a railway tire, equipped with a rocket engine.
“Unfortunately, the author of this idea remained unknown, as well as the details of the project.
It is not even clear whether a missile should have been used for overclocking or for braking the trolley.
Information about this drezina is known only from the press of that epoch.
Since 1933, the Polish Artillery began to think about missile arrows.
The study was carried out by the Armament Technology Section in cooperation with professors Mechislav Volfke and Gustav Mokzhitsky.
It is clear from the preserved materials that the studies have reached the stage of practical testing.
But with the advent of the German troops, the work was interrupted.
In 1937, a specialized seal came the idea of a photovoltaic fighter rocket, which was proposed by engineer Rogozinsky, and the next year the work “Intrudicre-Torpad missile and an aviation missile-bomb” of author Lelyva-Kyzhvioblotsky came out.
Both projects have been developed for the military use of rocket engines.
Before the very war, all the projects of military use of missile technology were carried out by the Temporary Scientific and Advisory Committee (Tymbassowy Komitet Dodradzo-Naukowy), which coordinated all the work.
The Committee was created in 1937, but after two years of its activity, the work ended due to the beginning of the war.
The next scientific work dedicated to cosmonautics, appeared in the Polish press after the war, thanks to the work of the Polish Astronautical Society (Polskie Towarzystwo Astronautyczne).
For the first time about the society is mentioned in the November issue of the 1954 magazine "Problems", which publishes four voluminous articles on Astronautics.
In one of them, Professor M. Subotovich proposed to organize a society that will be engaged in cosmonautics.
At that time, projects of artificial satellites were already gaining momentum, and it was clear that space research is a promising industry.
From the beginning of 1956 the Polish Astronautical Society (POA) tried to join the International Astronautical Federation (founded in 1951), and in the Autumn POA became a full member.
And in the following year, the first chairman of POA Kazimierz Zarankevich (1902 - 1959) became deputy chairman of the International Astronautical Federation.
In this position he remained until his death, which occurred in 1959.
Since the year of 1956 POA has made a significant contribution to the development of a very successful RM meteorological rocket (Rakieta Meteorologiczna), which became the first Polish missile to carry out a scientific research.
The first RM-1 type was completed in 1957, and the first launch took place on October 10, 1958.
Rocket, able to overcome a distance of 1800 m, was about 80 cm in length, and its weight was less than 5 bilgions.
Subsequently, an improved version of RM-1A was built, and in the summer of 1959 a twin-stage RM-2 missile was tested on Bledovsky Treadmill.
This missile was about 1.4 m in length, and its weight was about 11.5 kilograms.
The next version of the rocket was already able to engage in real scientific work - the RM-34 rocket could overcome 14.5 km, and its task was to observe the high-altitude wind.
But in 1962, further development was suspended.
The heiress of the first RM-type missiles was the Meteor-1 missile, developed between 1962 and 1965.
The missile was conceived as a two-stage, its total length was 510 cm, and the initial weight - 32.5 kg.
We developed three types (designated as Meteor-1A, -1B, and -1C), which differed in the size of the chamber for scientific equipment.
Rocket Meteor-1A had a space of 0.4 liter, Meteor-1B - 0.34 liters, and Meteor-1S - 0.62l.
The maximum flight range in all three types was 37 kilometers.
Between 1965 and 1968 at the Aviation Institute the Meteor-2 rocket was developed, and its first flight tests began in October 1970.
Rocket Meteor 2 with a starting weight of 380 kg was able to remove a payable cargo weighing 10 kilogram to a height of about 60 km.
Subsequently, Meteor-2N and Meteor-3 versions were built.
It is also worth mentioning Poland's accession to COSPAR (Committee on space exploration) in 1960 and the establishment of the national committee of COSPAR two years later.
In addition, as part as part of Intercosmos, Poland participated in the exploration of outer space on Soviet artificial satellites, and in in 1978 the Polish pilot Miroslav Germashevsky became the second inter-cosmotist after Vladimir Remek.
Repeated the law on public works is not a solution to the problem.
Last week the constitutional court annuled the law on public works.
The decree caused a lively discussion in society.
Undoubtedly, it will be interesting to look at this problem from a broader point of view.
Liberally oriented economy systems in the EU, as well as in a globalized world, are based on the principle of multiple, unregulated economic competition.
In essence, this means that individual economic subdivisions, national economic systems, are in a constant conflict with each other.
This is connected with the principle of free commerce and a free, unrestricted movement of private capital, along with unbridled financial specutulation.
As a result of a significant difference in the value of the labor force (wages), there is a price voltage.
Under this notion you need to understand a state where the manufacturer, through the delivery of a cheap product, tries to withstand in economic competition in the fact that it “confells” the cost of a competitor in order to take a large part of the market and, thus, to increase its own income.
On a massive scale, this means for the majority of Entrepreneurs either to move production abroad, either cheap purchases abroad or extinction. As a result, unemployment is risen in those in countries where the cost of the workforce, compared to others, is high.
Since the private capital does not bear any social responsibility, including for the unemployment produced by them, an unsustainable state spending on social negativities increases.
In general, the situation exacerbates the reluctance of Entrepreneurs to pay taxes and thereby to compensate for the social economic and social damage caused by them in pursuit of profit.
The situation is so well-fficient that there is no need to provide specific statistical data.
Unceremonious methods of private capital create at the level of the economies of individual states situations, when the governments of countries are forced to enter into competition with each other in order to artificially reduce the social level of their population in order to attract a foreign capital.
In other words, governments give their own population to private capital, regardless of social decline.
This is reflected primarily in the changes in the current legislation.
The goal is to economically complicate their people to subdue the diktat of private capital, first of all in the field of wages.
This acts as an economic coercion system in the event of prolonged equanciated unemployment and at the same time serves as an instrument to curtail the rights of workers in the field of labor legislation.
As a result, the level of poverty rises, and at the same time the difference between the poor and the rich.
In Germany for several years there has been a public distribution of products to the poor, which are not able to feed themselves with their own work.
The number of these people is already approaching a million.
As part of an increase in the competitiveness of the German economy, there are continued cases when employed people receive such a salary that the state must pay them extra in order for them to receive a subsistence minimum.
Such a scandal became known to the public and in the case of additional Bundestag employees.
Economic measures in almost all the southern states of the EU undoubtedly lead to the same condition in which people under the pressure of a disciplinary drop in social status are forced to either emigrate, as it was in the 19-th th century, or to live on a begret salary in the outskirts of society in the hope that private investment capital will one day come to the country.
However, it’s asked me, where will it come from?
If the capital comes from other EU countries, the pity will move from one country to another, or it won’t come at all, since the Chinese, the Indian, the Brazilian, the Turk, Moroccan, the Egyptian, the African is still working for a share of European wages.
This applies to the whole of Latin America.
Liberal theory and the media are nasty that the state cannot participate in the capital of its own economy, that a controlled economy leads to an economic catalysis.
Individual capital steadfastly insists that the state should not interfere in the economy.
Next, it is necessary to answer the question of whether private capital does not, now practically managing politics and the whole state, for its own selfish purposes?
Unequivocal answer - yes.
Evidentiary is the existence of almost omnipotentiary and omnipresent lobbies in all states.
As a result, we have a responsive situation manifested in corruption, ensuring mutual benefits, in legislation, where almost everything deserves to be penalized, but is not a crime.
In the Federal Agency of Germany, the situation is such that state-owned ministries due to a lack of financial resources are entrusted with the development of bills to private law firms that are closely associated with the industry.
Then these bills are approved by the Bundestag.
The entire government proceeds not from the people, according to the constitution of the Western type, but from financial-capacitated groups who prefer their own interests.
It is obvious that liberal-oriented democracy is now quickly found in such a situation, as described by the Appèganda in “Crisis of the Roman Rescense in the days of Caesar and Pompei”: “The state has been disintegrating for a long time, and departments are engaged in violence.
Bripples, Illegal Receiving Mercimony With Stones and Swords
Bribrupt and corrosion flourished without any prohibitions, and people went to the elections with a pre-sold voice. "...Descendant people did not run at all for the position of a ruler, in the aftermath of once the state for eight months was left without a consul" . . .
As in antiquity, in a modern society dominate their own responsibilities without taking into account public interests.
The private capital is already in its essence not intended for use for public purposes.
