“Operation “Argo”: when there is nowhere worse, call Hollywood
In November 1979, a mottle of Islamist demonstrator students sanctuated the U.S. Embassy in Tehran and took 52 diplomats hostage.
They had to be liberated in exchange for the ousted Shah Mohammad Reza Pahlavi, who escaped after the U.S. revolution, which had been the patron of his regime for decades.
For the U.S. administration, there was no positive exodization of the situation - she could not afford to throw Shah overboard, because this could fundamentally undermine the confidence of the allies in other countries.
However, it was not able to achieve the emancipation of the hostages in Iran, where the revolution led to the establishment of a theocratic regime, it was not possible.
This was a punch against the prestige of the U.S. that was later amplified by an unsuccessful attempt to free hostages by force.
Conclusive diplomats were finally vacated 444 days, after negotiations mediated by the Algerian government.
Their fate summoned homes a wave of solidarity and anti-Iranian sentiment.
Defeat in Iran contributed significantly to Jimmy Cartaire’s defeat in the 1980 presidential election that culminated in Ronald Reagan.
The film, staged by actor Ben Afflöck “Operation “Argo” describes one of the episodes of the story, which gave America small victories.
Shortly before the capture of the embassy, six workers managed to escape.
After difficult vicissitudes, they finished their journey at the residence of the Embassy of Canada.
The CIA in collaborating with Canadian authorities was able to take them out of Iran, with an extravagantuate cover legend, according to which they went on Canadian passports as members of the film crew, looking for a place to shoot a sci-phytic epic in the country.
Complication of Genre
the plan, which was invented by the “evacuation” expert Tony Méndez, demanded the cooperation of Hollywood.
In order for the legend to be reliable, in specialized journals it was written about the project of the film, press conferences were arranged, a fictitious manufacturing company had a real office.
Destinies of the operation for a long time were kept in a secret, the film, based on the memoirs of Tony Mendez.
Affleck's film is a special combination of several genres.
On the one hand, a real political thriller, the so-called "film-kinopus", the history of a successful idea, a scam - an example can be a number of films about Owsen's friends.
Motivations are continuing in the film - on the one hand, document-conceively conceived scenes from Tehran (in the credits show iconic historical photos of events and how the same situations have been demonstrated in the film - there are no big differences in this).
On the other hand, relieved Hollywood excrets intersecting with irony and moderate exaggeration.
And then the scenes from the headquarters of the CIA and other institutions - the men in costumes discuss the situation at the negotiating tables, on the stairs of the institutions, on the phone ...
Ben Affleck managed to make a career reboot reboot.
From the ridiculed actor became a terrified director, and his game ceased to be an object of ridicule.
“Operation “Argo” his third feature-length film, after the dark detective “Goodbye, Baby, Faste” (2007) and the thriller “City” (2010).
At the same time, this is the first Affleck film, which does not be shot in the director's hometown - Boston.
Feeling an atmosphere of place at the same time relates to the qualities that elevated the earlier films of the director to the Hollywood standard.
And Affleck manifests this in “Argo”, where Tehran “plays” Canada.
The best scenes of the film take place on the streets, during the refurbnament of real events - the introductory stages of the embassy fall immensatis themselves with their clarity, which also conveys the emotions of constituency, which occur when the story suddenly suddenly changes.
Afflek and his collaborators achieve a similar effect in fictitious stages (false-fashioned headquarters at the Tegheran bazaar).
Too many processes in too many places.
The Director had to deal with the fact that the narrative does not presuppose a lot of exciting skills of cinematographic importance.
He is quite successfully working with this a little, sometimes it comes up with something - it doesn't go so elegally (the scene in which a phone bell in America prevents an looming crisis at the airport of Tehran, and the chasurgitation on the runway looks quite contigniated).
Disadvantage "Argo" is absent-cash, associated with the need to reveal too many events in too many places.
Alan Arkkin and John Goodman in the role of Hollywood colleagues are indeed very charming, but their characters would deserve more space, and they in the film are far from the only ones.
Affleck's film lacks a bit of dramaticism, it's a film that you can watch with moderate interest, estimating the staging and a renetro stylist resorting the thrillers of the seventieth.
But it is difficult to grasp with difficulty.
However, this suffices to a reminder of one, still in a well-screatious sense of living history, as well as to testimonials about the omnipotentiary and omnipotentiary special services exaggerated.
Inflating rules of ball gloating, banana and circus
Portal www.bankovnipoplatky.com, which annually conducts a survey about the most absurd bank charges, now decided to announce a competition for “the most absurd decree or a project from an EU workshop”.
“We were prompted by the last event, in which the EU plans to adopt a 40 per cent quota for women in the administration of large European companies,” Patrick Naguger, an organizer of the questionnaire, told “Pravda”.
Among the insidiouscies that have already been nominated - the recent decision of the European Court to merge the rates of insurance premiums for men and women.
Until now, the women have had life security benefits, because for insurance companies they objectively are less likely to be at risk.
“Furniest incredible ideas from the EU workshop, people can nominate for the competition by the end of this year.
The vote itself will take place until the end of February 2013,” Naguer said.
Disclusive orders of the EU include, for example, the mandatory addition of biocomponentiants to fuel, which as a result is detrimental to nature, as well as a ban on the use of reliable merchandise thermograms only because they contain a relatively small number of dangerous substances, or a directive on the size of the cell for chickens, as a result of which this year has risen significantly in the price of eggs.
Also criticized was the de facto ban on the use of the term "screatine butter oil" or the removal from the sale of classic light bulbs.
Qualitative bananas should be 14 centimeters in length.
The pan-Turkish apparatus often makes a decision under the rapprochement of a particular commercial or industrial lobby whose positions in Brussels are usually protected by any state or a group of states (in this way, the Czech Republic is now even under the threat of filament to defend the demands of its banks).
The interests of the lobbies are as follows: for example, bananas of the highest quality in the European Union had to reach a length of 14 cm and did not dare to show “abnormal curvature”.
At the same time, the European Commission was arguided by harmonizing existing disparate national rules, which complicated trade.
The EU, despite the resistance of some states, still eased standards for fruits and vegetables, referring to the fact that existing directives will lead to waste of products.
The candidate for a win in the survey may also be last year's EU regulation, according to which sold balloons must necessarily be provided with a warning that children under the age of eight cannot indulge them unattended for adults.
The EU appealed to U.S. studies, according to which balloons during the game are a potential cause of death of children through suffocation.
Such a restriction now applies to children under the age of 14, who are prohibited from bleaching bunkers.
Funny ideas are born at home
Quite an assirdential rule concerning European officials themselves: everyone who has any official position in the EU cannot, taking into account the delicacitance of the topic for Greece, to use the name of Macedonia, but should instead say “BÜRM” (The Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia).
Portal Bankovípoplatky.com in cooperation with the association of liberal Economists “Laissez Faire”, proposed for a vote, in addition to several of these absurd rules mentioned above, for example, the EU regulation on the volume of food reserves in the territory of a member state.
The EU has established the maximum amount of food reserves that can be located in the territory of the Czech Republic on the day of its accession to the European Union.
Subsequent subsequently, the Czech Republic exceeded, for example, the established volume of canned mushrooms, for which she was threatened with a large fine.
The organizers of the interrogation were also interested and the idea of paying some countries for the fact that they do not have the sea, and the idea of granting subsidies for an appraisal to receive subsidiaries.
But these ideas originated in Praga, not in Brussels.
“We are at an unfavourable position, because we don’t have a sea.
Let’s ask the European Union for compensation”, – said in the autumn of 2004 the then Minister of agriculture Yaroslav Palas (CHSDP).
As an argument, he pointed out that the country had a high grain harvest, and as a result of the so-called inter-interventional proceeds, the state had complete inventories, which had to be removed.
For the fact that the Czech Republic is located far from the ports, the EU, according to Palas, had to pay us hundreds of millions of euros.
As a result, the European Commission went to meet the Czech Republic, organizing a tender for the purchase of grain from countries that are landlocked.
Subsidies to receive a subsidy were offered to the villages by the Ministry of Regional Development, headed by Minister Pavel Nemz (US-DEU), in particular, such subsidies had to go for an application for a subsidy from Brussel.
EU: bizardries are an exception
Although regulations in member states are easy to criticize it, the EU’s efforts to regulate, as well as more effective functioning and the development of the European Union, according to many of the experts, memorably deserve acknowledgment.
A serious problem, according to the experts, is to clutch EU grants for projects that do not even have a hint of anything in common with the deepening of European integration, but which the member states have achieved during the discussion of the budget.
Causes emotions among the Chekov and the fact that, as well as in other countries of the European Union, the Czech Republic must fight in Brussels for the right to a specific identification of its traditional products, and it does not always win in this competition.
Although after six years of fighting with the Germans and the Austrians retained the name "Olomouth Cheeses", but "Otmevsky rum", whose traditions in our country are rooted in the 19 century, our manufacturers had to be renegotiated to "Tuzemek".
rum can be called rubbish distillant, and not from sugar beet.
In the official list of registered products of the EU, along with the world-renowned chimists "feta" and "gorgondzola", a marzipan from the German Lübeck or Parma ham, already turned out to be, for example, carlovarian crackers, pogorzelitsky and Troshbona carp and zhitets hop.
Also, the trademark of the European Union can be proud of Pardubitz gingerberries and Gorzhitsky bulbs.
"People want me to protect the republic, but I'm an amateur," Okamura says.
The senator, how does a person come to the mind to run for the post of president?
I'm not thinking about becoming a senator or president.
If everything in our country functioned without problems, then I would not run anywhere.
But I can no longer see how over the last 20 years the country plunders, how thieves fuss, people raise taxes and the retirement age.
I didn’t have an ambivalence to be a politician.
But when I see something I don’t like, I’m trying to find a solution to how to change it.
And since I have already turned forty years and I am an independent person who does not treat any party, I do not have the opportunity to influencing things other than to run as a senator or a president.
You went to the Senate, but soon went to the presidential castle.
Don’t you turn your back in this way against the people who have chosen you?
I always said that I will join the struggle for the presidential castle, depending on the result of the election in the Senate.
Later, I clarified that if I was chosen as a senator, I will run for president.
My goal is not a position, a position is a tool with which I can fulfill my views.
Therefore, I need the greatest influence and the widest powers.
But the difficulty is not only that as a nation blushing in our own bar or at the TV, but at the same time we are ready to tramp anyone who will try to change something.
To this are the media that denigrate a person and who confuse freedom of speech with freedom of falsehood.
For example, they said about me that I am giving bribes to reporters, or that I was an adviser to Jiri Parowbek.
Let's move on to your views.
The struggle for the presidential castle you began with the theses about the material and criminal responsibility of politicians and the return property declarations in the amount of more than twenty million.
In order to do this, it is necessary to change the law.
You do not have such powers as a president, and only an entire senate can pronounce laws.
How do you want to solve this problem?
When I lobbied, as a citizen, I lobbied so that excursions became a free enterprise, it managed to promote it.
The problem lies in politicking - when someone comes with a good proposition from the left or on the right, he is intentionally obstructed, and this restrains the citizens.
As an independent non-participant, I have a much greater potential to gain support from all parliamentary parties.
“My advantage is that I cannot take advantage of every party settling on the shelf, without looking at the dogma, I can take from every party what is the best for our country and apply it.
Do you consider yourself a person who is more related to the right or to the left?
From the Czech point of view, it seems to me that people refer me rather to the left.
It doesn’t matter to me at all - a little to the left or a little to the right.
It’s important to me that we move forward.
We are not talking about the fact that someone relates to the right, but someone to the left, I want to unite people.
“I will always support any good solution for society to do if HRCM or GDP will propose it, and I’m going to be opposed to a bad idea.
You get angry when someone says that you're a populist.
Doesn’t you prove it by what you said?
When you’re creating a business plan for a firm, you’ve also had some perfect goals and views.
And you're trying to get closer to that.
We can call this populism, but all the sentences that I am talking about are already functioning in the world, or they are talked about by prominent experts.
But without the support of the parliament you will remain only slogans.
You won’t stay in politics for a long time.
or do you think that when you come to the people and talk with them, then you will be able to realize criminal and material responsibility?
I don't have another option.
Only to convince politicians, journalists, and the public and try to lure them to their side, so that we achieve ours.
If I were elected president, it would not be a problem to organize a live television broadcast, in which I will appeal to the chairmen of the parliamentary parties with an urging to legitimize material and criminal liability for politicians, civil servants, judges and procurators.
In case of refusal, they will have to report why they don’t want it.
If there is a strong person who announces abuses, then it will be possible to put pressure on a political scene.
Take the direct election of the President - it was a merit of pressure on the part of the public.
I speak directly that I’m a lover, not a genius or an intellectual.
“I’m trying to look for allies to defend my beliefs and views.
I'm only aspiring in politics, and I'm going to try to get the support of the majority.
I’m trying to promote things on my own; in the event that it does not work, in six years I will finish and go back to the private sector.
It sounds in part like Okamura must have saved the Czech Republic.
"I'm no savior.
I know I won’t do anything alone, so I’ve overtaken a number of well-known people with a proposal to run for the Senate.
I went to Radim Yanchura, he refused in connection with a large amount of work.
Also, I at least supported the leading investigative journalist Yana Lorentsova, who uncovered the scaffolding with light fuel oil products.
I put forward my candidacy because the people are really dissatisfied, but now I feel myself on the scale.
Sixty percent of people did not go to the forleation, and the majority of those who went elected representatives of the establishment.
There are only two of us independent in the Senate.
People have chosen the Senate in such a way that the changes will be carried out with difficulty.
In spite of this, I will fight for my views, such as the direct election of mayors and gubernators.
Do you think about the founding of your own party?
I didn’t think about it, because I don’t have the time to check the purity of every potential supporter’s past, and I don’t have money for it.
There is no money for the presidential campaign, there is only twenty thousand kroons in my transparent account.
You don't have any money?
You are talking about property declarations, but what is the state of your own business with this?
Personal property is valued at about $60 million.
I have a plot in Prague worth about $ 25 million, an apartment of 10 million, another apartment for $ 8 million, a collection of works of works of art for about 10 million, Aston-Martin for a 3.5-million dollar Aston-Martin and Skoda Superb for a million, and a few million more on account.
By the way Aston-Martin came up because it was my boyish dream - I've always liked Jemes Bond, who drove a car, was a gray for women and at the same time struggled against meanness and law-free.
Do you travel to Aston Martín, do you own 60-munder property and you don't have money for the campaign?
You say that you want to change the republic, but you don’t really want to invest your own money.
It's not very conclusive.
I don't have $15 million for the campaign.
Do I have to get into debt?
I’ve already invested 2.5 million in the campaign.
The fact that I don’t have any sponsors indicates that my program isn’t so interesting.
I don’t have to pay for an election campaign out of pocket.
Expenditures on the campaign will actually be covered by senatorial salary.
But with this money, I would not live, for example, I could not pay my son for an English school, which costs 30 thousand monthly.
If only I wanted to make money, I wouldn’t be running anywhere.
Will you continue to be engaged in entrepreneurship, so you can live?
Didn’t you tell me you’re going to shorten it?
But this does not depend on the size of the salary.
As I promised, I partially reduced my activities.
For example, the managing director of the tourism agency in the spring will be my deputy.
People would like that I was an unscrupulous who will keep the republic.
But I need to live on something, too.
How much, as an entrepreneur, are you accustomed to receive monthly?
from two hundred to four hundred and four hundred thousand, what I get further.
And even if I became president, I would have graduated from entrepreneurship.
