However, Pilata Fatulaeva (48) is convinced that in Lerika there is something to interest tourists.
“In May, Baku became famous for Euro-Visibility song festival – and next year we will hold a festival of the oldest people in the world,” Fatulaeva said.
She is the director of the Longevity Museum, probably the only one in the world.
The biography of about eight dozen of these places is documented, which is more than 100 years old. Fatulaeva indicates a black-and-and-beat photo.
It's my grandpariitation, he's here 120 years old.
At the age of 136, he had another child
But the dissolutory star of the museum is Chabana Shiraly Müslyumov, who allegedly turned 168 years old.
The birth certificate, however, does not exist.
And taking into account the fact that the oldest person, whose age is confirmed by the documents, turned 122 years, Müslyumov's age seems extremely dubious.
“He was born in this area in 1805, he died in 1973,” Explains Fatulaeva.
The man was Married three times, and he had 23 children, at the age of 136 he allegedly had a daughter.
So did Chaban Müslyumov added a couple of decades to his age?
After all, even Rembrandt Scholz, an age researcher at the Max Planck Institute in Rostock, has heard about centenarians in Central Asia.
Amazingly, a lot of elderly people can also be found in some areas of China, in Japan or the Hunza Valley in Pakistan,” Scholz said, “Early a lot of very old people also live in Sardinia.”
However, due to the absence of documents, the scientific confirmation of age is impossible, since there have been no registers of civil status.
every day a glass of corpse butter
Nevertheless, there is a fact that people in the Lerik area often reach biblical age.
Now there are 20 people older than the age of 100 lives here.
Why there are so many centencies here in the south?
The Azerbaijani tour guide Farid Mugimzade understands this with the special genes of the Talyshes.
The director of the Fatulayeva museum, on the contrary, believes that it is a matter of nutrition.
Tayles love meat, bread and most dairy products, many of them drink a glass of drizzled oil every day. However, it is unlikely that such a high-calorie diet can be healthy from a dietary point of view.
Or it's a primordial way of life, who keeps people's youth? In Chengemiran, a tiny village near the city of Lerik, Rubaba Mirzoev lives.
At the age of '97, it is still relatively young for these latitudes.
Myrzageva, who claims that she has 143 descendants, lives in a mere wooden house, which is typical for the entire Caucasian region.
She sits on the floor with a barrel of the butter, which tirelessly rides back and forth.
There are eight people living under the same roof, including one of his sons and daughter Mirzayeva, who have arguer for a long time.
Two children are also riding nearby.
In the Kitch, guests are prepared tea, which is served in the typical vulnerable glasses of Armuda.
Myrzaeva has perfectly smooth and steadfast white teeth, under a headscarf, she hides long dark breeze, which her son proudly reveals to us.
I'm always my hair with milk, so they've never fallen out and kept the color.
“And I’ve never used shampoo,” Mirzayev said.
Mon-to-hosted a monthly pension
She always harbored only what grew up in her own yard, tomatoes, potato peas.
I've never bought groceries at the store in my life.
Then she talks about her husband, who served in an army.
The most difficult was after the Second World War.
But it has become better, when "favorite father" Heydar Aliyev stood at the helm.
Propaganda doesn't often sound like an old-fashioned woman.
However, the cult, created around the figure of the father of the nas, who ruled the country as a dictator, practically does not know the borders in Azerbaijan.
He remained in power until 2003, then his son Ilham accepted the reins of power.
Nevertheless, there is no poverty among the Azerbaijani elders.
230 manats (approximately equal to the same amount of the euro), Mirzayev receives monthly as a pension, for local conditions this is an amount for which you can live well.
And, it is a long-groughted son of Mirzaeva also right: "The Elders in our culture have deep respect."
They live in a large family, are loved, surrounded by care and are happy.
