Unexpected Consequences
While the fall in the birth rate has a certain effect on the nation's economic growth, tax revenues, spending on medicine and immigration policy, the example of Singapore also begins to have some unexpected consequences.
The government makes an effort to ensure that so many small housing is not being built.
For example, this began to influencing the real estate sector.
